    "change_set": {
      "schema": "adaos.builder.change_set.v1",
      "change_set_id": "builder-change-set-865e54b17c74496d8149219aac1347bc",
      "request": "Implement and validate the Builder Lifecycle projection fix in builder_sdk_control_skill. Requirements: 1. Project Lifecycle is one dependent lineage. Prototype/revision is the root. Automation appears beneath its source Prototype only when there is an actual handoff, durable task, retained result/snapshot, or a meaningful non-idle state. phase/status values idle, not_started, empty, or a default projection alone are not evidence and must return no Automation child. 2. Never fall back to the Prototype semantic version for a nonexistent idle Automation. A newly created scenario such as test04_recipes must project exactly one Prototype node before handoff. 3. Publication is not an independent root. When published evidence exists, nest it beneath the Automation that produced it; mark inferred legacy lineage explicitly rather than silently attaching it to the current result. 4. Keep Prototype UI revision labels distinct from artifact semantic versions and keep preview labels explicit with proto:, active:, and public: prefixes. 5. Read scenario semantic version and metadata from scenario.yaml only. scenario.json must never override it. 6. Preserve current functional tool schemas and UI compatibility. Add focused regressions for a new 0.1.0 scenario with default idle Automation, a real Automation task, and Publication nesting. Check consistent modified timestamp formatting where Lifecycle metadata is projected. 7. Run the complete builder_sdk_control_skill tests and validation. Commit through the normal Forge checkpoint after tests pass. Do not publish and do not push remote repositories beyond that governed DEV checkpoint.",
